# Prefer blades over React

This repo has two marquee/slider implementations. **Blades is the product.** React is a leftover prototype. Do not change React unless the user explicitly asks to update the React version.

## Edit these

- Markup / content: `index.html` (CMS blade HTML)
- Enhance / carousel / DOM: `src/blades/enhanceTableauMarquee.ts`
- Slide chrome (frame, cards, media, icons): `src/blades/slideChrome.ts`
- Blade-only CSS: `src/blades/tableauMarquee.css`
- Shared motion: `src/slider/calloutMotion.ts`
- Shared backgrounds: `src/slider/backgrounds.ts`
- Shared visual CSS used by blades: `src/Slide/Slide.css`, `src/Carousel/Carousel.css`, `src/App.css`

Entry: `src/main.tsx` already mounts React **and** calls `enhanceTableauMarquee()`. Keep that blades call. Do not remove or bypass it.

## Do not edit (unless asked)

- `src/App.tsx`
- `src/Carousel/Carousel.tsx`
- `src/Carousel/carouselData.ts`
- `src/Slide/Slide.tsx`

If a request sounds like “the slider”, “slides”, “callouts”, “cards”, “hero”, or “marquee”, implement it in blades + shared CSS/motion only.

## Inline Figma images

This blades layout can ship **only CSS and JS**. Do not add Figma assets as files under `public/` or as extra image URLs.

- Put Figma SVGs, icons, frames, and backgrounds **inline** in CSS or JS (data URIs or markup strings). See `src/slider/backgrounds.ts`.
- Raster Figma exports (PNG/WebP) also go inline as `data:image/...` in CSS or JS.
- CMS slide/callout media in `index.html` is authored content — leave those URLs. Everything from Figma is chrome and must travel inside the CSS/JS bundle.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — extra file we cannot ship
el.style.backgroundImage = "url(/bg.svg)"

// ✅ GOOD — inlined in JS/CSS
el.style.backgroundImage = `url("data:image/svg+xml,${encodeURIComponent(svg)}")`
```
